  "tour.scubadive.result.bent_line": "  %1$s: decompression sickness (total x3/4)",
  "message.scubadive.center.missing_gear": "Tours need: %s (wear mask, BCD, wetsuit and fins, dive computer on the wrist slot, camera and light in your inventory)",
  "guide.scubadive.toc": "Contents",
  "guide.scubadive.prev": "Previous page",
  "guide.scubadive.next": "Next page",
  "guide.scubadive.sites.detail": "Depth %s-%s m",
  "guide.scubadive.page.intro.title": "Welcome",
  "guide.scubadive.page.intro.body": "Dive, photograph sea life and fill your own field guide.\nThis book covers gear, buoyancy, air, photos, tours and dive centers. Use the arrows or the contents to turn pages.",
  "guide.scubadive.page.gear.title": "Gear",
  "guide.scubadive.page.gear.body": "Mask (head), BCD with cylinder (chest), wetsuit (legs), fins (feet, faster swimming).\nMask + BCD with air left: you can breathe underwater.\nFull set: hostile mobs ignore you.",
  "guide.scubadive.page.bcd.title": "BCD & buoyancy",
  "guide.scubadive.page.bcd.body": "M = inflate (rise), N = deflate (sink).\nBCD air shrinks as you go deeper, so keep adjusting. Green on the dive computer means neutral: it saves air and scores better photos.",
  "guide.scubadive.page.bcd.c1": "Rise",
  "guide.scubadive.page.bcd.c2": "Neutral",
  "guide.scubadive.page.bcd.c3": "Sink",
  "guide.scubadive.page.tank.title": "Tank pressure",
  "guide.scubadive.page.tank.body": "A full cylinder holds 200 bar; on tours you get 100 bar.\nDeep, fast or out-of-trim swimming uses more. Hovering or resting on the bottom saves air. Refills in about 10 s at the surface (not on tours).",
  "guide.scubadive.page.ascent.title": "Rapid ascent",
  "guide.scubadive.page.ascent.body": "After going below 8 m, rising too fast shows a warning. Ignore it and you get decompression sickness at the surface.\nDeflate the BCD and come up slowly.",
  "guide.scubadive.page.ascent.c1": "Slow",
  "guide.scubadive.page.ascent.c2": "Too fast",
  "guide.scubadive.page.computer.title": "Dive computer",
  "guide.scubadive.page.computer.body": "Put it in the wrist slot (above the off-hand slot) or hold it.\nIt shows dive time, depth, max depth, tank pressure, BCD air and buoyancy. Green means neutral.",
  "guide.scubadive.page.light.title": "Dive light",
  "guide.scubadive.page.light.body": "Hold it to light the way ahead.\nBrighter subjects score higher in photos. A must in caves, wrecks and deep water.",
  "guide.scubadive.page.camera.title": "Camera & photos",
  "guide.scubadive.page.camera.body": "Left click: photo mode (left click again to leave)\nWheel: zoom\nRight click: shoot\nJ: field guide (Wild / Tour), where you can review your photos.",
  "guide.scubadive.page.score.title": "Photo score",
  "guide.scubadive.page.score.body": "Points come from centring, size, groups, distance (haze), your buoyancy, light, silt and angle (from behind scores less). Rarer creatures are worth more. Get close rather than zooming.",
  "guide.scubadive.page.hazards.title": "Watch out",
  "guide.scubadive.page.hazards.body": "Sharks, barracuda and morays bite back if attacked. Crown-of-thorns and urchins prick. Jellyfish sting.\nCorals break if you crash into them; fast swimming over sand stirs up silt.",
  "guide.scubadive.page.guide.title": "Field guide",
  "guide.scubadive.page.guide.body": "Dozens of kinds of sea life live in the oceans, lakes and dive sites. Photograph one to add it to your field guide (J); your best score for each is kept.",
  "guide.scubadive.page.guide2.title": "Field guide (2)",
  "guide.scubadive.page.guide2.body": "Big ones like mantas and whale sharks cruise open water; tiny ones like pygmy seahorses and nudibranchs hide on corals and rocks. Look closely!",
  "guide.scubadive.page.center.title": "Dive center",
  "guide.scubadive.page.center.body": "A hut with a pier on beaches, snowy beaches and stony shores.\nClerk: buys fish (also small fish in buckets) for emeralds and sells gear.\nGuide: tour reception.",
  "guide.scubadive.page.tour.title": "Tours",
  "guide.scubadive.page.tour.body": "Pay the guide in emeralds to sign up; friends join at the same guide and the host starts. A boat takes you to the dive site.",
  "guide.scubadive.page.tour.c1": "Sign up",
  "guide.scubadive.page.tour.c2": "Boat",
  "guide.scubadive.page.tour.c3": "Dive",
  "guide.scubadive.page.tour.c4": "Return",
  "guide.scubadive.page.tour.c5": "Ranking",
  "guide.scubadive.page.tour_rules.title": "Tour rules",
  "guide.scubadive.page.tour_rules.body": "- One 100 bar cylinder, no refills.\n- The dive ends when you climb back on the boat, or when you surface with 10 bar or less.\n- Running out of air halves your score.\n- Decompression sickness and broken coral cost points.\n- Rankings are shown at the end.",
  "guide.scubadive.page.sites.title": "Dive sites",
  "guide.scubadive.page.sites.body": "Each site has its own creatures and depth. Price: emeralds per diver.",
  "guide.scubadive.page.commands.title": "Commands",
  "guide.scubadive.page.commands.body": "/scubadive trench\nShows the nearest deep trench; click the coordinates for a teleport command.\n\n/locate structure scubadive:dive_center\nFinds the nearest dive center.\n\nHappy diving!",
